From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: James Kane <jkane@tds.net>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 07:53:33 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 14/14] [VectraOS] one timer sleeper in the global executor

One idle thread waits for the soonest deadline (the timer sleeper), the
rest for a packet alone, so a deadline wakes one thread, not all of them
(each a migration in croi, then contention for the queue's lock). A
deadline set from one of the queue's own threads wakes no one: that
thread takes the role when its job ends. A sooner deadline revokes the
holder (a generation number) and wakes a sleeper to take it up; a thread
leaving with a job while deadlines wait and no one holds the role wakes
one to. Suggested by croi; 50 back-to-back sleeps cost about 330 context
switches rather than 515, the median lateness the same (VectraOS's M6f).
---
 .../Concurrency/VectraOSGlobalExecutor.cpp    | 52 +++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 47 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

